WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.084
Two missiles can reach the same far-off

2
00:00:02.084 --> 00:00:03.896
target in very different ways.

3
00:00:03.896 --> 00:00:05.649
One is thrown like a ball;

4
00:00:05.649 --> 00:00:07.748
the other flies like a small plane.

5
00:00:08.148 --> 00:00:10.122
A ballistic missile is powered only for

6
00:00:10.122 --> 00:00:12.003
a short time at the start.

7
00:00:12.003 --> 00:00:14.034
Most of its flight is unpowered:

8
00:00:14.034 --> 00:00:16.879
it coasts along a high arc and

9
00:00:16.879 --> 00:00:18.804
then falls onto its target.

10
00:00:19.204 --> 00:00:21.956
An intercontinental ballistic missile climbs more than

11
00:00:21.956 --> 00:00:23.511
a thousand kilometres,

12
00:00:23.511 --> 00:00:24.394
far above the air,

13
00:00:24.394 --> 00:00:25.773
before it falls.

14
00:00:26.174 --> 00:00:29.088
A cruise missile works differently.

15
00:00:29.088 --> 00:00:30.946
Its engine runs through the flight,

16
00:00:30.946 --> 00:00:32.165
wings give it lift,

17
00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:33.813
and it steers itself,

18
00:00:33.813 --> 00:00:35.716
often flying very low.

19
00:00:36.115 --> 00:00:37.915
So the ballistic missile rises high and

20
00:00:37.915 --> 00:00:39.110
falls fast.

21
00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:41.839
The cruise missile stays inside the atmosphere

22
00:00:41.839 --> 00:00:43.845
and is harder to spot coming.

23
00:00:44.246 --> 00:00:46.208
India has both.

24
00:00:46.208 --> 00:00:47.926
In March twenty twenty-four,

25
00:00:47.926 --> 00:00:52.083
Mission Divyastra tested Agni-Five carrying several warheads

26
00:00:52.083 --> 00:00:54.033
aimed at different targets.

27
00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:55.914
BrahMos is a cruise missile developed with

28
00:00:55.914 --> 00:00:56.853
Russia.

29
00:00:57.252 --> 00:00:58.274
For GS Three,

30
00:00:58.274 --> 00:01:00.305
ask two questions of any missile:

31
00:01:00.305 --> 00:01:02.186
is it powered all the way,

32
00:01:02.186 --> 00:01:04.054
and does it leave the atmosphere?

